[[Opening card: 3 seconds. CHAIN OF CUSTODY. AI-generated drama.]]

DR. NAOMI BELL is a fictional Black woman in her late thirties, a federal-court evidence auditor in a cream coat. SGT. WADE HOLLIS, about fifty-five, has run the county records room for fourteen years. DEPUTY ELI MORENO, about twenty-six and six months on the job, wears a body camera. CALVIN REED, about forty-five, appears only in the last scene.

A plain courthouse records room: a long counter with an open ledger, a desk and computer behind it, two waiting chairs by the wall, shelves of archive boxes, one hallway door. No other person is seen or heard. There is no music.

INT. LINWOOD COUNTY COURTHOUSE - RECORDS ROOM - MORNING

[[SC01 — The sign-out log]]

NAOMI is standing at the customer side of the counter; HOLLIS is standing behind the records counter; ELI is standing beside the hallway door. Props are preset between scenes; no other visible or audible people.

[[SC01_g01 ACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Naomi sets the sealed brown packet flat on the counter beside the open ledger and lifts her hands away.

[[SC01_g02 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Morning, Sergeant. I need one exhibit logged out to room 3B.

[[SC01_g03 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
That's a court seal. Nobody brought anything like that in here.

[[SC01_g04 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
I sealed it downstairs this morning, after the inventory was finished.

[[SC01_g05 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Downstairs is my property room. Who let you in down there?

[[SC01_g06 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
The same court order you signed for six weeks ago, Sergeant.

[[SC01_g07 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
I signed for an inventory. Counting boxes. Not carrying things out.

[[SC01_g08 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Nothing's leaving the building. It goes upstairs to 3B by eleven.

[[SC01_g09 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Then it goes in my ledger first, with what's inside it.

[[SC01_g10 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
The ledger asks for an exhibit number. Not for contents.

[[SC01_g11 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
In this room, the ledger asks what I tell it to.

[[SC01_g12 REACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Eli watches from beside the hallway door, the small green light of his body camera steady, his face carefully neutral.

[[SC01_g13 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Deputy, is your camera running? I'd like it to keep running.

[[SC01_g14 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
It runs the whole shift, ma'am. I don't switch it off.

[[SC01_g15 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Nobody asked you, Moreno. Stand where you're standing and stay quiet.

[[SC01_g16 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Exhibit number is on the tape. Forty-one dash seventeen dash A.

[[SC01_g17 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
I can read tape. I'm asking what that seal is protecting.

[[SC01_g18 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
It's protecting the contents from everyone who isn't the grand jury.

[[SC01_g19 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Grand jury. In my building, and nobody thought to tell me.

[[SC01_g20 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Nobody is supposed to tell you. That's what sealed means, Sergeant.

[[SC01_g21 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Then it sits right here until somebody tells me something true.

[[SC01_g22 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
It's ten forty now. I'm expected upstairs in twenty minutes, Sergeant.

[[SC01_g23 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Then you'd better start talking. Twenty minutes is all you've got.

[[SC01_g24 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
I'll talk. But nothing I say will be about what's inside.

[[SC01_g25 ACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Hollis closes the ledger and rests one hand flat on its cover.

INT. LINWOOD COUNTY COURTHOUSE - RECORDS ROOM - MORNING

[[SC02 — Whose rule]]

NAOMI is standing at the customer side of the counter; HOLLIS is standing behind the records counter; ELI is standing beside the hallway door. Props are preset between scenes; no other visible or audible people.

[[SC02_g01 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Start with your name. Everybody who signs this ledger gives one.

[[SC02_g02 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
My name is on the court order in your file drawer.

[[SC02_g03 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
I'm not opening drawers. I'm asking you, standing at my counter.

[[SC02_g04 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Naomi Bell. Evidence auditor, under contract to the federal court.

[[SC02_g05 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Federal. So somebody downtown sent you here to count my boxes.

[[SC02_g06 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
A judge sent me. I've counted every box, and every shelf.

[[SC02_g07 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Six weeks in my basement, and I never heard your name.

[[SC02_g08 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
That was deliberate. People behave normally when nobody knows who's watching.

[[SC02_g09 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
You hear that, Moreno? She's been watching us. Write that down.

[[SC02_g10 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
Write down what, Sarge? She hasn't done anything I can write.

[[SC02_g11 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
You write what I tell you. That's what a report is.

[[SC02_g12 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
If you doubt me, call the grand jury clerk. Extension four-one-one.

[[SC02_g13 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
I don't call upstairs because a stranger hands me a number.

[[SC02_g14 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Then call the switchboard and ask for 3B. Same answer, Sergeant.

[[SC02_g15 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
I've worked this building fourteen years. I know who belongs here.

[[SC02_g16 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
You know who used to belong. Things changed six weeks ago.

[[SC02_g17 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
What changed six weeks ago? Go on, say it plainly.

[[SC02_g18 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
A judge ordered an audit. That's plain. That's all I'll say.

[[SC02_g19 REACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Hollis studies her face for a long moment, jaw tight, saying nothing.

[[SC02_g20 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Put some identification on the counter. Then we'll see what's plain.

[[SC02_g21 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
You'll get my ID. You won't get what's under the seal.

[[SC02_g22 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Moreno, if she walks out with that, you stop her. Understood?

[[SC02_g23 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
Stop her how, Sarge? She hasn't broken any rule I know.

[[SC02_g24 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
She's breaking mine. In this room, that's the one that counts.

[[SC02_g25 ACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Naomi takes a plastic ID card from her coat pocket and places it on the counter next to the packet.

INT. LINWOOD COUNTY COURTHOUSE - RECORDS ROOM - MORNING

[[SC03 — The ID on the counter]]

NAOMI is standing at the customer side of the counter; HOLLIS is standing behind the records counter; ELI is standing beside the hallway door. Props are preset between scenes; no other visible or audible people.

[[SC03_g01 ACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Hollis picks up the ID card from the counter and holds it close to read it.

[[SC03_g02 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Bell. Washington address. You drove four hours to count boxes?

[[SC03_g03 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
I drove four hours every Monday. I left every Friday afternoon.

[[SC03_g04 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
And slept where? Not anywhere in this county, or I'd know.

[[SC03_g05 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
The motel by the interstate. Room twelve. Check that too.

[[SC03_g06 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Sit down over there. This takes as long as it takes.

[[SC03_g07 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
It takes about a minute. I'll stand, if that's all right.

[[SC03_g08 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
It isn't all right. Chairs are right there. Use one.

[[SC03_g09 ACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Naomi sits down in one of the two waiting chairs by the wall, her eyes still on the packet.

[[SC03_g10 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
Ma'am, would you like some water? There's a cooler outside.

[[SC03_g11 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
No, thank you. I'd rather nobody leaves the room right now.

[[SC03_g12 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
Understood. Then I'll stay right here by the door, ma'am.

[[SC03_g13 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Funny. A woman alone, sealed packet, worried about who leaves rooms.

[[SC03_g14 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Not funny. Careful. You'd want the same if it were yours.

[[SC03_g15 REACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Hollis types at the computer behind the counter, then stares at the screen without blinking.

[[SC03_g16 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
No warrants. No tickets. Not one parking violation. Nothing at all.

[[SC03_g17 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
That's usually what it says about people who mind their business.

[[SC03_g18 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Or people who know how to keep their names off screens.

[[SC03_g19 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
You'd know more about keeping names off records than I would.

[[SC03_g20 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
What's that supposed to mean? Say it again for the camera.

[[SC03_g21 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
I said nothing that isn't already true. The camera heard it.

[[SC03_g22 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
Sarge, her record's clear. Normally we'd hand back the card now.

[[SC03_g23 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Normally isn't today. The card stays with me until I'm done.

[[SC03_g24 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Keep the card. It changes nothing about the seal, Sergeant Hollis.

[[SC03_g25 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
We'll see. Fifteen minutes is long in a small room.

INT. LINWOOD COUNTY COURTHOUSE - RECORDS ROOM - MORNING

[[SC04 — Names he shouldn't know]]

NAOMI is seated in a waiting chair by the wall; HOLLIS is standing behind the records counter; ELI is standing beside the hallway door. Props are preset between scenes; no other visible or audible people.

[[SC04_g01 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Let me guess. This started with Ray Pruitt, didn't it?

[[SC04_g02 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
I'm not going to talk about anyone by name, Sergeant.

[[SC04_g03 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Property tech. Quit in August. Hired a lawyer the same week.

[[SC04_g04 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
People hire lawyers for all kinds of reasons. Mostly ordinary ones.

[[SC04_g05 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Not Ray. Ray couldn't afford coffee. Somebody paid for that lawyer.

[[SC04_g06 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
You've thought about this a great deal, haven't you, Sergeant?

[[SC04_g07 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
A records request has sat on my desk for three weeks.

[[SC04_g08 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Three weeks is long for a records request. Most take days.

[[SC04_g09 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Most aren't asking for every property log from twenty-seventeen.

[[SC04_g10 REACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Eli glances from Hollis to Naomi, then down at the floor, uneasy.

[[SC04_g11 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
You haven't answered it. That's what three weeks usually means.

[[SC04_g12 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
I answer when I'm ready. Downstairs runs on my schedule.

[[SC04_g13 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
It used to. For six weeks, it ran on mine.

[[SC04_g14 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Is it Pike Street? Or Delmar? Just tell me which one.

[[SC04_g15 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
I haven't mentioned a single case. You've mentioned two already.

[[SC04_g16 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Calvin Reed. That's the one, isn't it? Somebody's crying about Reed.

[[SC04_g17 REACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Naomi keeps her face completely still, hands folded in her lap, giving nothing back.

[[SC04_g18 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Reed was nine years ago. The jury took forty minutes.

[[SC04_g19 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
I'm not here to argue about any jury. Only about paper.

[[SC04_g20 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Paper. You think paper can hurt fourteen years of my work?

[[SC04_g21 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Paper doesn't hurt anyone. It remembers what people did to it.

[[SC04_g22 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
Sarge, maybe we just let her go up. She's expected.

[[SC04_g23 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Maybe you just go stand in the hall if you're nervous.

[[SC04_g24 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
I'm not nervous. I'm only saying she's been patient with us.

[[SC04_g25 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Patient people are the ones you watch, Moreno. Remember that one.

INT. LINWOOD COUNTY COURTHOUSE - RECORDS ROOM - MORNING

[[SC05 — First warning]]

NAOMI is seated in a waiting chair by the wall; HOLLIS is standing behind the records counter; ELI is standing beside the hallway door. Props are preset between scenes; no other visible or audible people.

[[SC05_g01 ACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Hollis slides the sealed packet across the counter toward himself and keeps his hand flat on top of it.

[[SC05_g02 ACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Naomi rises from the waiting chair and steps back to the counter.

[[SC05_g03 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Please take your hand off that. It isn't in your custody.

[[SC05_g04 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Everything in this room is in my custody. That's my job.

[[SC05_g05 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Not this. This was sealed by order of a federal judge.

[[SC05_g06 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Then the judge can come down and tell me so himself.

[[SC05_g07 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Herself. And she would, but you won't like how it goes.

[[SC05_g08 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
You think I scare easy? I've been in worse rooms.

[[SC05_g09 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
I don't want you scared. I want you to hear me.

[[SC05_g10 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Go on, then. I'm listening. Moreno's camera is listening too.

[[SC05_g11 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
If that seal breaks in your hands, it can't go back.

[[SC05_g12 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Wax is wax. Anybody can buy a stick of red wax.

[[SC05_g13 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
The wax isn't the point. The tape and the form are.

[[SC05_g14 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Everyone who touches that packet signs the form. Times, names, reasons.

[[SC05_g15 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
So I sign it too. Sergeant Hollis, opened for review. Simple.

[[SC05_g16 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
That's exactly what it would say. Forever, on every copy.

[[SC05_g17 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Signatures. You people and your signatures. Like ink ever proved anything.

[[SC05_g18 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
You keep talking like you know what's inside better than me.

[[SC05_g19 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
I do know. I wrote most of it. That's the difference.

[[SC05_g20 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Then there's nothing in there you can't just tell me yourself.

[[SC05_g21 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
I can't tell you. I'm warning you. Those are different things.

[[SC05_g22 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Sounded like a threat. Moreno, did that sound like one?

[[SC05_g23 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
It sounded like a warning, Sarge. She said it real calm.

[[SC05_g24 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Calm. Everybody's calm until the paper's out on the table.

[[SC05_g25 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
The paper's already on the table. You're the one holding it.

INT. LINWOOD COUNTY COURTHOUSE - RECORDS ROOM - MORNING

[[SC06 — Eli's line]]

NAOMI is standing at the customer side of the counter; HOLLIS is standing behind the records counter; ELI is standing beside the hallway door. Props are preset between scenes; no other visible or audible people.

[[SC06_g01 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Moreno, get your notebook out. We're writing this up right now.

[[SC06_g02 ACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Eli takes a small notebook from his chest pocket and holds it closed in one hand.

[[SC06_g03 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Subject refused to identify contents of an unlogged item. Write that.

[[SC06_g04 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
She gave her name, Sarge. And the exhibit number. It's logged.

[[SC06_g05 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Not in my ledger, it isn't. So it's unlogged. Write it.

[[SC06_g06 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
I can write that she asked to log it. That's true.

[[SC06_g07 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
You've been here six months. You don't decide what happened, son.

[[SC06_g08 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
The camera decides, Sarge. That's what you told us in training.

[[SC06_g09 REACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Hollis turns slowly to look at Eli, surprised, his mouth tightening.

[[SC06_g10 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
I told you a lot. Pick the parts that help you.

[[SC06_g11 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Deputy Moreno. You don't have to write anything you didn't see.

[[SC06_g12 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
Ma'am, with respect, please let me handle my own sergeant.

[[SC06_g13 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Fair. Then I'll ask one thing. Please don't stop that camera.

[[SC06_g14 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
I already told you. It runs the whole shift. That's policy.

[[SC06_g15 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Policy. You both love policy until it's your name on something.

[[SC06_g16 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
I'd like my identification back now, Sergeant. You've checked it.

[[SC06_g17 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
You'll get it back when that packet's logged properly.

[[SC06_g18 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Then write it in properly. Exhibit number, time, my signature, done.

[[SC06_g19 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
And contents. My ledger has a contents column. Always has.

[[SC06_g20 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Your ledger has a column for sealed items too. Page one.

[[SC06_g21 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
She's right, Sarge. There's a sealed column. I've seen it used.

[[SC06_g22 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Moreno, one more word and you're working nights till Christmas.

[[SC06_g23 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
Yes, Sarge. But the column's still there either way.

[[SC06_g24 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Fine. Then the seal comes off, and the column won't matter.

[[SC06_g25 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
You say that like it's decided. It doesn't have to be.

INT. LINWOOD COUNTY COURTHOUSE - RECORDS ROOM - MORNING

[[SC07 — Second warning]]

NAOMI is standing at the customer side of the counter; HOLLIS is standing behind the records counter; ELI is standing beside the hallway door. Props are preset between scenes; no other visible or audible people.

[[SC07_g01 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Who are you working for? Internal affairs? A defense firm?

[[SC07_g02 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
I work for the court. I've said that three times now.

[[SC07_g03 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Courts don't send auditors for nothing. Somebody complained. Who complained?

[[SC07_g04 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Nobody complained to me. I counted. Counting doesn't need a complaint.

[[SC07_g05 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Counting what? Boxes? I count boxes every Friday. They're all there.

[[SC07_g06 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
The boxes are all there. That isn't what I was counting.

[[SC07_g07 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Then what? Bags? Weights? Signatures? Just tell me what you counted.

[[SC07_g08 REACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Naomi looks at him steadily and says nothing, letting the question hang in the room.

[[SC07_g09 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Signatures. You were counting my signatures. That's what this is.

[[SC07_g10 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Guess all you like. I'm not answering any of it here.

[[SC07_g11 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
That's not a no. Moreno, you heard. That wasn't a no.

[[SC07_g12 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
It wasn't a yes. I'm declining a question you can't ask.

[[SC07_g13 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
I can ask anything I want in my own records room.

[[SC07_g14 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
You can ask. You can't open. That's where the line is.

[[SC07_g15 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Lines. Everybody's got lines for me today. Nobody's got answers.

[[SC07_g16 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Here's an answer. It's ten fifty-two. I'm still standing here.

[[SC07_g17 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
I could have walked out ten minutes ago. I didn't.

[[SC07_g18 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Because Moreno would've stopped you. I told him to stop you.

[[SC07_g19 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Because walking out breaks the chain. I don't break the chain.

[[SC07_g20 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
So you need my signature. You need me. Say it.

[[SC07_g21 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
I need a clean record. Your signature is part of it.

[[SC07_g22 ACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Hollis picks up the packet from the counter and turns it over in both hands, studying the seal.

[[SC07_g23 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Second time, Sergeant. Opening that won't end what you're afraid of.

[[SC07_g24 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
It will finish it. With your own hands, on camera.

[[SC07_g25 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
My camera? That's Moreno's camera. Moreno works for me. Not you.

INT. LINWOOD COUNTY COURTHOUSE - RECORDS ROOM - MORNING

[[SC08 — What a seal is for]]

NAOMI is standing at the customer side of the counter; HOLLIS is standing behind the records counter; ELI is standing beside the hallway door. Props are preset between scenes; no other visible or audible people.

[[SC08_g01 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
I hand-carried one of these once. Federal seal. Twenty-eleven, I think.

[[SC08_g02 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Then you remember how careful everyone was. Nobody touched the seal.

[[SC08_g03 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
The captain made me sign three times between car and courtroom.

[[SC08_g04 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Three signatures for one envelope. Did you wonder why, back then?

[[SC08_g05 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
I figured lawyers like paperwork. Lawyers always like their paperwork.

[[SC08_g06 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
It's not for lawyers. It's for the accused. And the accuser.

[[SC08_g07 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
A seal means nobody added anything, and nobody took anything away.

[[SC08_g08 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
And you're telling me nobody's taken anything away from this one.

[[SC08_g09 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Not since I signed it at nine. Read the form yourself.

[[SC08_g10 REACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Hollis tilts the packet to read the custody form taped to its back, the form turned away from the camera, lips moving silently.

[[SC08_g11 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Bell, nine-oh-four. Bell, ten-thirty-eight. That's all it says. Just you.

[[SC08_g12 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Just me. So everything inside is exactly as I left it.

[[SC08_g13 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
Ma'am, can I ask something? What happens if somebody opens it?

[[SC08_g14 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Then the next line on that form gets their name.

[[SC08_g15 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
And the grand jury asks why. The answer goes on record.

[[SC08_g16 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
Even if they just look? Even if they put it back?

[[SC08_g17 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
There's no straight back, Deputy. The wax breaks once. Only once.

[[SC08_g18 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
She wants you scared, Moreno. It's a performance. Don't buy it.

[[SC08_g19 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
I'm not scared, Sarge. I'm trying to understand what we're doing.

[[SC08_g20 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
What we're doing is our jobs. Somebody in this room should.

[[SC08_g21 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
My job ends when that packet reaches 3B, seal whole.

[[SC08_g22 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
And when does my job end? When your paper says so?

[[SC08_g23 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
I can't answer that. I only know where mine ends.

[[SC08_g24 ACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Hollis sets the packet back down on the counter but keeps one hand resting on it.

[[SC08_g25 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Eight minutes. You've got eight minutes, and so have I, apparently.

INT. LINWOOD COUNTY COURTHOUSE - RECORDS ROOM - MORNING

[[SC09 — Third warning]]

NAOMI is standing at the customer side of the counter; HOLLIS is standing behind the records counter; ELI is standing beside the hallway door. Props are preset between scenes; no other visible or audible people.

[[SC09_g01 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Here's what I think. You want me to be afraid.

[[SC09_g02 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Afraid men hand things over. I've watched it for years.

[[SC09_g03 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
I don't want anything handed over. I want you to stop.

[[SC09_g04 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Stop what? Asking questions in my own room? Doing my job?

[[SC09_g05 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Stop before your hands do something your head hasn't decided yet.

[[SC09_g06 REACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Hollis glances toward Eli and the doorway, as though measuring who is watching him.

[[SC09_g07 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Moreno's watching. The camera's watching. Everyone wants to see me blink.

[[SC09_g08 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Nobody wants you to blink. I'd rather you just walked away.

[[SC09_g09 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Walk away and wait for a call? I've waited three weeks.

[[SC09_g10 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Three weeks of nobody calling. Every morning, waiting for that phone.

[[SC09_g11 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
I know. That part I'm sorry about. Waiting is hard.

[[SC09_g12 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Don't you dare feel sorry for me. Not in my building.

[[SC09_g13 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
Sarge, please. Let her sign it out. It's not too late.

[[SC09_g14 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Right is me knowing what's coming before it lands.

[[SC09_g15 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
This is the third time I'm saying it. Don't open that.

[[SC09_g16 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Whatever you think is in there, opening it is worse.

[[SC09_g17 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Believe you. A stranger who spent six weeks in my basement.

[[SC09_g18 ACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Naomi takes one deliberate step back from the counter and lets her hands hang at her sides.

[[SC09_g19 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
I won't reach for it again. It's yours now, Sergeant.

[[SC09_g20 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Mine. Good. That's the first thing you've said that makes sense.

[[SC09_g21 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Moreno, note the time. Ten fifty-four. Sergeant Hollis reviewing contents.

[[SC09_g22 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
I'm noting the time, Sarge. And that she warned you.

[[SC09_g23 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Note whatever you want. You'll see I was right about her.

[[SC09_g24 ACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Hollis picks up the packet with both hands and slides one thumb under the edge of the red wax seal.

[[SC09_g25 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Ten fifty-four. I'll remember that time for a long while.

INT. LINWOOD COUNTY COURTHOUSE - RECORDS ROOM - MORNING

[[SC10 — The seal]]

NAOMI is standing one step back from the counter; HOLLIS is standing behind the records counter; ELI is standing beside the hallway door. Props are preset between scenes; no other visible or audible people.

[[SC10_g01 ACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Hollis presses his thumb under the wax until the red seal cracks and comes away from the paper.

[[SC10_g02 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Ten fifty-four. Exhibit forty-one, seventeen, A. Seal broken by Sergeant Hollis.

[[SC10_g03 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Say it like a newsreader if you want. It's just wax.

[[SC10_g04 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
Sarge, you actually did it. You actually broke a federal seal.

[[SC10_g05 ACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Hollis draws a thin stack of papers halfway out of the packet, keeping the pages face down on the counter.

[[SC10_g06 REACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Hollis lifts the top page close to read it, its printed side turned away from the camera, and the color slowly drains from his face.

[[SC10_g07 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
Sarge? What does it say? You've gone completely white, Sarge.

[[SC10_g08 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
It's a grand jury cover sheet. Linwood County property room investigation.

[[SC10_g09 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
The line underneath it names the subject of the investigation.

[[SC10_g10 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
Whose name, Sarge? Tell me whose name is on that page.

[[SC10_g11 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
It's a mistake. Somebody typed this wrong. This is all wrong.

[[SC10_g12 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Nobody typed it wrong. I checked that line three times.

[[SC10_g13 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Six cases. I logged thousands of bags. Thousands of them.

[[SC10_g14 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Six where the weights changed before trial. Your signature both times.

[[SC10_g15 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Signatures get copied. Anybody could have signed my name on those.

[[SC10_g16 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Ray Pruitt watched you sign them. He kept copies nine years.

[[SC10_g17 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Ray. Of course it's Ray. He never could keep quiet.

[[SC10_g18 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Ray kept quiet nine years. That's the part that broke him.

[[SC10_g19 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
Ma'am, is that why you needed it sealed? Because of him?

[[SC10_g20 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
It's sealed because every page has to reach the jury untouched.

[[SC10_g21 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Now it reaches them with one new page. His.

[[SC10_g22 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
I didn't write anything. I opened an envelope. That's all.

[[SC10_g23 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
On camera. After three warnings. In front of a deputy.

[[SC10_g24 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Moreno. Turn that thing off. Just for one minute. Off.

[[SC10_g25 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
I can't, Sarge. You know I can't. And I won't.

INT. LINWOOD COUNTY COURTHOUSE - RECORDS ROOM - MORNING

[[SC11 — Who makes the call]]

NAOMI is standing one step back from the counter; HOLLIS is standing behind the records counter; ELI is standing beside the hallway door. Props are preset between scenes; no other visible or audible people.

[[SC11_g01 REACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Hollis stands motionless behind the counter, staring down at the opened packet, both hands flat on the counter edge.

[[SC11_g02 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Reed. Calvin Reed is one of the six, isn't he?

[[SC11_g03 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
He's the first of the six. Nine years in Barlow State.

[[SC11_g04 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
The bag weighed what it weighed. I wrote what was there.

[[SC11_g05 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
At intake it was eleven grams. At trial, it was fifty-two.

[[SC11_g06 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Eleven grams is a misdemeanor. Fifty-two was nine years. Your handwriting.

[[SC11_g07 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
You think a number on a form says who I am?

[[SC11_g08 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
No. But it tells a jury what a man did.

[[SC11_g09 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
What happens now, ma'am? What am I supposed to do?

[[SC11_g10 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
That's your call, Deputy. Not mine, and not his. Yours.

[[SC11_g11 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Moreno. Eli. Listen to me. Think about your career.

[[SC11_g12 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Six months in. Make this call and nobody here trusts you.

[[SC11_g13 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
Sarge, you taught us the camera decides. It already decided.

[[SC11_g14 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
I was talking about other people, son. Not about us.

[[SC11_g15 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
There isn't an us, Sarge. There's just what the camera saw.

[[SC11_g16 ACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Eli unclips the radio from his shoulder and raises it close to his mouth.

[[SC11_g17 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI (INTO RADIO)
Records to 3B. Sealed exhibit opened at the counter. Clerk, please.

[[SC11_g18 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
They knew she was coming, Sarge. They've been waiting since ten.

[[SC11_g19 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
Two marshals are coming down. The clerk wants you upstairs.

[[SC11_g20 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Upstairs. Fourteen years, and I've never once been called upstairs.

[[SC11_g21 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
You can walk up yourself, Sergeant. Nobody has to walk you.

[[SC11_g22 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

HOLLIS
Is that a kindness? From you? After everything you've just done?

[[SC11_g23 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
It's the last choice you still get to make yourself.

[[SC11_g24 ACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Hollis walks out from behind the counter and leaves through the hallway door without looking back.

[[SC11_g25 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Deputy, log it with me. Opened at ten fifty-four.

INT. LINWOOD COUNTY COURTHOUSE - RECORDS ROOM - AFTERNOON

[[one month later]]

[[SC12 — A month later]]

NAOMI is standing at the customer side of the counter; ELI is standing behind the records counter. Props are preset between scenes; no other visible or audible people.

[[SC12_g01 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
Doctor Bell. I didn't think we'd see you down here again.

[[SC12_g02 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Just one more signature. The grand jury released the exhibit back.

[[SC12_g03 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
Two signatures now, for everything. Mine and the clerk's. New rule.

[[SC12_g04 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Good rule. Sounds like somebody who learned something. Who wrote it?

[[SC12_g05 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
The oversight board. I asked them to keep the sealed column.

[[SC12_g06 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
How are things here? Honestly. Not the version for the board.

[[SC12_g07 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
Quiet. Some people don't talk to me. Most people do, actually.

[[SC12_g08 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
And Sergeant Hollis? I heard about the indictment, not much else.

[[SC12_g09 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
Suspended. His certification's gone. Trial's set for March, they're saying.

[[SC12_g10 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
He sent me a note. Said I wrote the report right.

[[SC12_g11 REACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Naomi takes that in quietly with a small, tired nod.

[[SC12_g12 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
That might be the truest thing he's written in years.

[[SC12_g13 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
Four of the six cases are vacated. Two more by Christmas.

[[SC12_g14 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
And Mr. Reed? I was told he'd be down here today.

[[SC12_g15 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
Any minute. He's coming for his property envelope. Nine years shelved.

[[SC12_g16 ACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Calvin Reed enters through the hallway door and walks slowly to the customer side of the counter.

[[SC12_g17 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

CALVIN
They said upstairs to come here for my things. Calvin Reed.

[[SC12_g18 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

ELI
Yes, sir. It's ready. Watch, wallet, keys. Everything's logged.

[[SC12_g19 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

CALVIN
You're Doctor Bell. My lawyer said you read every page twice.

[[SC12_g20 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
Three times, Mr. Reed. Some pages I couldn't stop reading.

[[SC12_g21 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

CALVIN
Nine years I said the weight was wrong. Nobody listened.

[[SC12_g22 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
It's written down now. In a place nobody gets to change.

[[SC12_g23 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

CALVIN
I don't know what to say to you. I keep trying.

[[SC12_g24 DIALOGUE — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

NAOMI
You don't owe me anything. Sign for your things. They're yours.

[[SC12_g25 ACTION — native 6s / intended used 5.5s]]

Calvin picks up the pen from the counter, signs the ledger slowly with the page out of focus, then sets the pen down.

